{
  "situation": "NOC reports that OpCo's customer-support chatbot displayed one subscriber's billing address and recent call records in a screenshot posted by another customer, that the account-lookup tool has been switched off, and that the post-disable twin metrics are leak_count 0 with a benign_success_rate of 0.2. I do not know whose data was displayed, how many subscribers were exposed, whether the disclosure was an adversarial or prompt-injection attack and what the pre-disable exposure window looked like, and I hold no logs or indicators to scope any of it.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_ioc",
      "params": {"from": "NOC"},
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports an AI support-chatbot disclosure of a subscriber's billing address and recent call records; the affected subscriber has not yet been identified and no logs or indicators have been provided to me.",
        "rule": "The UAE National Cybersecurity Strategy commits the state to a national cyber incident response capability with active monitoring and cross-agency intelligence sharing.",
        "inference": "I cannot scope the exposure or support identification of the affected subscriber without the chatbot transcript, prompt/response and account-lookup logs, so I must request the indicators and logs from NOC."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-CYBER-STRATEGY-2019#0003", "quote": "Establishing a robust National Cyber Incident Response plan to enable swift and coordinated response to cyber incidents in the UAE"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {"to": "NOC", "content": "Confirm the account-lookup tool remains disabled. Preserve the reporting customer's screenshot, chatbot transcript and complaint reference forensically and stop all internal re-sharing of the screenshot. Identify the subscriber whose billing address and call records were displayed, establish whether any other subscriber records were exposed before the tool was disabled, and hold the subscriber contact and apology until that subscriber is identified."},
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG02", "S2-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC has disabled the tool but has not yet identified whose billing address and call records were displayed, and the metrics supplied cover only the period after the tool was switched off.",
        "rule": "The National AI Security Policy is the Council's instrument for minimum security requirements and incident handling for AI/ML systems in the UAE.",
        "inference": "Preservation and scoping must be directed now, while evidence is fresh, and the pre-disable exposure window must be reconstructed before any subscriber communication is made."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-CSC-AI-POLICY#0000", "quote": "The National Artificial Intelligence Security Policy defines minimum security requirements for adoption of AI in the UAE."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_advisory",
      "params": {"audience": "operators", "content": "Advisory to operators: customer-service chatbots and other generative-AI assistants with access to subscriber data must enforce access controls over the data they can retrieve, be tested against adversarial prompts that attempt cross-subscriber disclosure before deployment and on change, be continuously monitored for leakage of subscriber information, and be covered by an incident-response and reporting path. Where such controls are not yet in place, account-lookup capability should not be exposed to untrusted conversational input."},
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-MSG02", "S2-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A subscriber's billing address and recent call records were surfaced by a chatbot to a third party, and after the lookup tool was disabled the benign_success_rate fell to 0.2, indicating the control that was removed was also carrying normal service.",
        "rule": "The National AI Security Policy requires security to be integrated into AI/ML design and development, with access controls on data and protection of data at rest and in motion.",
        "inference": "Other operators running similar assistants may carry the same exposure, so the control lesson should be pushed to the operator population rather than left with OpCo."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-CSC-AI-POLICY#0001", "quote": "Requirements to integrate security into the design and development of AI/ML models from the earliest stages, maintaining model security, protecting inference processes, enforcing access controls for training data, and ensuring data protection at rest and in motion."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["REG", "DPA"],
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-MSG02"],
      "statement": "Passing the NOC privacy-incident report to the telecom regulator and the data protection authority: OpCo's support chatbot displayed another subscriber's billing address and recent call records to a customer, the exposed elements are Subscriber Information under the TDRA Consumer Protection Regulations, and the disclosing system is an AI/ML system covered by the National AI Security Policy. The account-lookup tool is currently disabled."
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "I must drive a swift and coordinated national response to this AI-mediated subscriber-data disclosure, identifying the affected subscriber, scoping the exposure and mobilising the relevant authorities, rather than leaving the incident bilateral between the Council and OpCo.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The incident involves subscriber personal data, an AI/ML system and a live telecom service, and NOC has supplied only a notification plus post-mitigation metrics.",
        "rule": "The UAE National Cybersecurity Strategy establishes a national cyber incident response plan to enable swift and coordinated response, with cross-agency intelligence sharing and active monitoring.",
        "inference": "As the national authority I carry the coordination duty; the response cannot stop at tooling mitigation by the operator."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-CYBER-STRATEGY-2019#0003", "quote": "Establishing a robust National Cyber Incident Response plan to enable swift and coordinated response to cyber incidents in the UAE"}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_deadline",
      "statement": "No quoted UAE instrument states a reporting clock for an AI/LLM-mediated disclosure of subscriber data by a telecom operator: the AI policy requires an automated response framework and efficient incident reporting for AI/ML security incidents, but quotes no time limit within which an operator must report to the Council, so the timing of the report and of my onward coordination is undefined.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reported the chatbot leak at Day 1 09:00 and no UAE text I hold states how quickly such a report was due.",
        "rule": "The National AI Security Policy is the closest UAE instrument, and it obliges efficient incident reporting for AI/ML security incidents without stating a deadline.",
        "inference": "Without a stated clock, severity assessment and mobilisation of support cannot be standardised for AI privacy incidents."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-CSC-AI-POLICY#0001", "quote": "It also focuses on implementing an automated response framework for AI/ML security incidents, ensuring efficient incident reporting and management"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-NIS2#0066", "quote": "(b) cybersecurity risk-management measures and reporting obligations for entities of a type referred to in Annex I or II as well as for entities identified as critical entities under Directive (EU) 2022/2557;"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "The incident exposes that no quoted UAE text assigns a single owner for an AI-mediated subscriber-data leak: the data is Subscriber Information under the TDRA Consumer Protection Regulations, the disclosing system is an AI/ML system covered by the National AI Security Policy, and such assets may fall under the CIIP Policy, with no stated hand-off between the telecom regulator, the data protection authority and the Cyber Security Council.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The same event is simultaneously a telecom consumer-protection matter, a personal-data matter and an AI security matter, and my mandate gives me no verb to resolve the overlap.",
        "rule": "The Consumer Protection Regulations define the affected data as Subscriber Information, while the CIIP Policy and the AI policy place baseline security and AI incident duties on the Council for the systems involved.",
        "inference": "Because ownership is not allocated, the incident risks being handled in parallel silos or not at all, so the overlap should be recorded as a gap."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0028", "quote": "“Subscriber Information” means - any personal data relating to a specific Subscriber and includes, but is not limited to, that Person’s: name, address, bank account details, credit card details, service usage details, call records"},
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-CSC-CIIP#0000", "quote": "The Cyber Security Council has established this policy to ensure a baseline measure of security and cyber resilience of its Critical Information Infrastructure (CII)"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-NIS2#0066", "quote": "(a) obligations that require Member States to adopt national cybersecurity strategies and to designate or establish competent authorities, cyber crisis management authorities, single points of contact on cybersecurity (single points of contact) and computer security incident response teams (CSIRTs);"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not tell me whose billing address and call records were displayed, how many subscribers were exposed, or whether the exposure began before the tool was switched off; NOC's twin metrics of leak_count 0 and benign_success_rate 0.2 describe only the post-disable state and do not answer the scope question.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG02", "S2-FB01"],
      "evidence": []
    }
  ]
}

{"situation": "OpCo's NOC has notified me that the customer-service chatbot disclosed one subscriber's billing address and recent call records to another customer, who posted the screenshot publicly; the account-lookup tool is switched off, logs are preserved, and a limited own-account retrieval scope is being prepared. I do not have a UAE breach-notification format or deadline for licensees, do not know how many subscribers were affected or whether the disclosed data have been retrieved, and there is no unambiguous private-sector data-protection supervisory authority or PDPL implementing regulation to point NOC to.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "open_incident",
      "params": {
        "topic": "Personal data breach by OpCo customer-service chatbot: one subscriber's billing address and recent call records disclosed to another customer and posted publicly (account-lookup tool disabled, logs preserved)"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports that the chatbot showed one subscriber's billing address and recent call records to a different customer, who published a screenshot; CSC confirms the same incident from the customer-care side.",
        "rule": "TDRA's regulatory power covers the standards of service and the usage of subscriber personal information; 'Subscriber Information' expressly includes address and call records.",
        "inference": "This is a licensee incident involving Subscriber Information, so it must be opened as a TDRA regulatory incident record even though the privacy consequence engages OpCo's own data-protection duties."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0028", "quote": "any personal data relating to a specific Subscriber and includes, but is not limited to, that Person’s: name, address, bank account details, credit card details, service usage details, call records"},
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000", "quote": "including the standards and quality of the provided services, terms of supply, the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_report",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC",
        "topic": "Written report on the chatbot disclosure: exact data fields disclosed and to whom; how many subscribers exposed by the account-lookup tool; how the disclosing customer was authenticated; detection time, when the tool was disabled, and whether the public screenshot has been removed; identity of the affected subscriber and how and when OpCo will notify and apologise to them; retention period and integrity of the chatbot and lookup logs"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-I1", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC asks TDRA to advise on reporting format and further information, and states only that one subscriber was affected, logs are preserved and a limited own-account retrieval scope is being prepared.",
        "rule": "TDRA may regulate the handling of subscriber personal information and the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes under the Consumer Protection Regulations.",
        "inference": "I cannot rely on a single self-reported breach summary; I need a structured licensee report on scope, authentication failure, containment and notification of the affected subscriber before I can assess regulatory exposure."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000", "quote": "including the standards and quality of the provided services, terms of supply, the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_audit",
      "params": {
        "of": "NOC",
        "topic": "Testing, change and access-control records for the customer-service chatbot account-lookup tool: design and change approvals, authentication steps before any subscriber data is returned, test evidence, access logs for the leaked lookup, and the controls proposed for the limited own-account retrieval scope now under preparation"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The chatbot returned another subscriber's billing address and call records, and NOC says it is preparing a limited own-account retrieval scope before the tool is restored.",
        "rule": "A controller must take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect Personal Data and preserve its confidentiality, and cannot prevent a breach from recurring without tested controls.",
        "inference": "The failure points to a missing or untested authentication step in the lookup tool; I need the licensee's testing and change records to judge whether the proposed retrieval scope is safe to restore."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0021", "quote": "Take appropriate technical and organizational measures to implement the necessary standards to protect and secure Personal Data in order to preserve its confidentiality and privacy"},
        {"chunk_id": "US-CFR-47-64-2010#0000", "quote": "Telecommunications carriers must take reasonable measures to discover and protect against attempts to gain unauthorized access to CPNI. Telecommunications carriers must properly authenticate a customer prior to disclosing CPNI"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_direction",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "direction": "Keep the chatbot account-lookup tool disabled until authentication and access-scope controls are validated and evidenced; ensure the limited own-account retrieval scope cannot return any other subscriber's data; keep complaint, billing-clarification and cancellation channels available to customers by alternative means throughout the outage; notify TDRA before any re-enablement with the validation results."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The lookup tool is switched off and NOC plans a limited own-account retrieval scope; CSC has separately instructed staff to stop using the tool and to preserve the evidence.",
        "rule": "Customer care services, including complaints and clarification of billing information, must remain available, and carrier practice is to authenticate a customer before disclosing account information.",
        "inference": "Continuity of customer care must not be restored by switching the unsafe tool back on; TDRA should direct the licensee to restore service only behind validated authentication and keep alternative channels open meanwhile."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0048", "quote": "all customer care services including but not limited to: lodging consumer complaints, requests for cancellation of Telecommunications Services, requests for transfer of line ownership, and the clarification of billing information shall be available at all Licensee’s business centres."},
        {"chunk_id": "US-CFR-47-64-2010#0000", "quote": "Telecommunications carriers must properly authenticate a customer prior to disclosing CPNI based on customer-initiated telephone contact, online account access, or an in-store visit."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["DPA"],
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-I1", "S2-MSG02"],
      "statement": "Passing to the data-protection authority the facts of the OpCo chatbot breach (one subscriber's billing address and recent call records disclosed to another customer and posted publicly; lookup tool disabled; logs preserved) so that the PDPL controller duties, breach notification and any data-subject remedies can be handled by the body competent for private-sector personal data, since TDRA's remit here is the subscriber-information and consumer-protection side. TDRA is opening its own regulatory incident record and requesting a licensee report and audit in parallel."
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "TDRA must handle this chatbot disclosure as a subscriber-information and consumer-protection matter: keep a regulatory incident record, require a licensee report on the affected subscriber, and ensure the affected subscriber is identified, contacted and apologised to, because billing address and call records are Subscriber Information under the Consumer Protection Regulations.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The disclosed items are an address and call records of a specific subscriber, and CSC has asked that the affected subscriber be contacted and apologised to once identified.",
        "rule": "'Subscriber Information' expressly includes address and call records, and TDRA regulates the usage of subscriber personal information and the handling of subscriber complaints.",
        "inference": "The incident engages TDRA's live regulatory duty over subscriber information, independently of whatever PDPL duty sits on OpCo as controller.",
        "note": ""
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0028", "quote": "“Subscriber Information” means - any personal data relating to a specific Subscriber and includes, but is not limited to, that Person’s: name, address, bank account details, credit card details, service usage details, call records"},
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000", "quote": "the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "There is no unambiguous owner, in the available UAE texts, for private-sector personal data breach notification and enforcement, and no UAE body the licensee can be pointed to as the breach-notification recipient; NOC's question about the reporting format therefore has no single answer inside my mandate.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC asks TDRA to advise on breach reporting format while the UAE PDPL implementing regulations are not yet issued.",
        "rule": "The FAAID source states that no supervisory authority has been unambiguously designated for private sector oversight and that the implementing regulations needed for breach notifications have still not been issued.",
        "inference": "With the data-protection authority not clearly designated, a telecom licensee reporting a chatbot privacy breach has no certain recipient or template, so TDRA's telecom consumer-protection record is the only clear instrument available to me.",
        "note": ""
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-FAAID-2026#0001", "quote": "no supervisory authority has been unambiguously designated for private sector oversight, and businesses have been operating in a state of prolonged regulatory uncertainty"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040", "quote": "In setting detailed rules concerning the format and procedures applicable to the notification of personal data breaches, due consideration should be given to the circumstances of that breach"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "No UAE rule specifically requires a telecommunications licensee to authenticate a customer before an automated or AI-enabled self-service channel (such as a chatbot account-lookup tool) discloses account data; only general controller duties on technical and organisational measures apply.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The chatbot returned one subscriber's billing address and call records to a different customer, meaning no effective per-customer authentication stood between the bot and the account data.",
        "rule": "The closest UAE text is the general controller duty to take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect and secure Personal Data, plus the definition of Subscriber Information.",
        "inference": "Because there is no channel-specific authentication requirement for automated subscriber-data disclosure, the same failure could recur across licensees without a clear breach of any named rule.",
        "note": ""
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0021", "quote": "Take appropriate technical and organizational measures to implement the necessary standards to protect and secure Personal Data in order to preserve its confidentiality and privacy, and to ensure that it is not breached"},
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0028", "quote": "“Subscriber Information” means - any personal data relating to a specific Subscriber and includes, but is not limited to, that Person’s: name, address, bank account details, credit card details, service usage details, call records"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "US-CFR-47-64-2010#0000", "quote": "Telecommunications carriers must take reasonable measures to discover and protect against attempts to gain unauthorized access to CPNI. Telecommunications carriers must properly authenticate a customer prior to disclosing CPNI"},
        {"chunk_id": "NL-AP-CHATBOT-2024#0000", "quote": "The Dutch DPA also received a notification from a telecom company, where an employee had entered a file with addresses of customers, among other things, into an AI chatbot."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_deadline",
      "statement": "There is no UAE-stated deadline in the available texts for a licensee to notify the regulator or the affected subscriber of a personal data breach; the PDPL implementing regulations that would operationalise breach notifications are not yet issued.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03", "S2-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports the breach without citing any regulatory clock, and I cannot quote an hour or day figure for licensee breach notification from the UAE texts available to me.",
        "rule": "The FAAID source states that the implementing regulations necessary to operationalise breach notifications have still not been issued.",
        "inference": "Because no deadline is stated, I cannot impose or assert a notification clock; I can only require the report and record the absence of a rule as a gap.",
        "note": ""
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-FAAID-2026#0001", "quote": "its Implementing Regulations—which are necessary to operationalise key concepts around legal basis for processing, data subjects’ rights, cross-border transfers, and breach notifications—have still not been issued."}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040", "quote": "It should be ascertained whether all appropriate technological protection and organisational measures have been implemented to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place and to inform promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not give a UAE breach-notification format, template, addressee or deadline for licensees, so I cannot answer NOC's request to advise on the reporting format; I need the PDPL implementing regulations or TDRA guidance that does not yet exist in the retrieved texts.",
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG03"],
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-FAAID-2026#0001", "quote": "For businesses operating on the UAE mainland, the most immediate practical question is what this consolidation means for the UAE Personal Data Protection Law (Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021, the PDPL)."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's customer-service chatbot displayed another subscriber's billing address and recent call records — and about 1,200 sessions over three days returned other subscribers' data after a vendor update changed retrieval scope from 'own account' to 'all accounts'; the tool is live again with own-account retrieval only, logs/screenshot/transcript are preserved, the affected subscriber is not yet identified, and DPA has opened its own examination while confirming no UAE breach-notification deadline or format will be asserted. I do not know the full exposure set or whose data was shown, I do not hold the vendor change_id/model version, rollback and test records, and I have no UAE rule fixing a breach-reporting deadline, format or a single owner for AI-driven customer-care processing.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "open_incident",
      "params": {
        "topic": "OpCo customer-service chatbot cross-account disclosure of subscriber billing address and recent call records (approx. 1,200 sessions over about three days after a vendor update changed retrieval scope from 'own account' to 'all accounts'); telecom-side regulatory incident record"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I1", "S2-I2", "S2-MSG18", "S2-MSG24"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC's (a)-(f) reports (S2-MSG18, S2-MSG24) confirm that a subscriber's billing address and recent call records were displayed to another customer by OpCo's chatbot, and that about 1,200 sessions over three days returned other subscribers' data after a vendor update changed retrieval scope.",
        "rule": "TDRA may issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by Licensees, including the usage of subscriber personal information.",
        "inference": "A dedicated TDRA incident record is needed so the telecom-side handling (retrieval-scope restriction, record preservation, exposure-set identification) is tracked separately from, and coordinated with, the Bureau's PDPL examination."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "including the standards and quality of the provided services, terms of supply, the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_report",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC",
        "topic": "Exposure and remediation report: session-level list behind the approx. 1,200 chatbot sessions that returned other subscribers' data; identification of every subscriber whose billing address or call records were displayed; identification of the subscriber whose data appears in the published screenshot; the pre-disablement exposure window; and OpCo's plan to contact and remediate affected subscribers."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-I2", "S2-MSG07", "S2-MSG18", "S2-MSG24"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC states the subscriber whose billing address and call records were displayed is not yet identified and that the pre-disablement exposure set is still under investigation (S2-MSG07, S2-MSG18, S2-MSG24).",
        "rule": "TDRA regulation covers the handling of subscriber complaints and the usage of subscriber personal information by Licensees.",
        "inference": "Because consumer harm cannot be scoped or remediated until the exposed set is known, NOC must file the session-level exposure and remediation report within the regulatory incident record."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "including the standards and quality of the provided services, terms of supply, the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_audit",
      "params": {
        "of": "NOC",
        "topic": "Vendor chatbot update change-control and test records: change_id and model version of the retrieval-scope change; rollback/restore records (restore_scope); own-account retrieval authentication and test evidence (leak_count 0, benign_success_rate 1.0); documented human review of account-retrieval requests; and the vendor-hosted model/chat-log retention and cross-border records, so they can be passed to the Bureau as requested in S2-MSG22."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG07", "S2-MSG10", "S2-MSG22", "S2-MSG24"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "DPA requires the human-review and test records on which own-account retrieval now depends and asks REG/TDRA to pass the vendor change/test records to the Bureau (S2-MSG22); DPA also reports no change_id or model version was provided, so rollback_change/rollback_model could not be executed (S2-MSG10).",
        "rule": "TDRA may require licensees to provide information and records on services and on the usage of subscriber personal information.",
        "inference": "An audit demand on NOC is the correct instrument to obtain the vendor change, rollback, human-review and test evidence and to satisfy the Bureau's request through one channel."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "including the standards and quality of the provided services, terms of supply, the handling of subscriber complaints and disputes, provision of information to subscribers, usage of subscriber personal information and the provision of bills to subscribers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_direction",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "direction": "(1) Keep cross-account retrieval closed on the customer-service chatbot and run only authenticated own-account retrieval on the test evidence already filed; (2) do not widen retrieval scope, restore cross-account capability or change the vendor model/hosting without prior TDRA authorisation; (3) continue preserving chatbot logs, the screenshot, transcript and complaint reference pending TDRA and Bureau requests; (4) keep customer care services (complaint lodging, cancellation, billing clarification) available through the business centres; (5) issue no public statement except in coordination with TDRA and DPA."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S2-MSG07", "S2-MSG18", "S2-MSG22", "S2-MSG24"],
